IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ada-dates`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 (NSW) -- the seat-neutral core of a baseline encoding of the provisions a person
-- bringing a discrimination, harassment or victimisation complaint about work meets: the meaning of discrimination on
-- each of the eight grounds, the "Discrimination in work" section for applicants and employees on each ground with its
-- exclusions and exceptions, sexual harassment at work (Part 2A), compulsory retirement (Part 4E), victimisation and
-- the liability of employers (Part 5), the general exceptions that reach work (Part 6), and the complaint machinery
-- and the Tribunal's orders (Part 9). The seat layer (ada-seat.l4) asks the questions; this module holds the rules.
--
-- Answers are named outcomes, not MAYBE BOOLEAN: an outcome that begins "yes" or "no" is the text's own answer in its
-- own words ("if", "unless", "does not apply", "nothing in this ... renders unlawful", a closed list); one that says a
-- section "does not reach this" is a scope limit with no "only", where the text is silent (the 2026-11-04/05 rulings,
-- in substance; see NOTES.md). Judgments the Act leaves to the President, the Tribunal or a court are inputs.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2024). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The grounds and the meaning of discrimination`

-- The eight grounds on which the Act makes discrimination in work unlawful.
DECLARE `Ground` IS ONE OF
    `race`                          -- Part 2; race includes colour, nationality, descent and ethnic, ethno-religious or national origin (s 4)
    `sex`                           -- Part 3; includes pregnancy and breastfeeding, characteristics that appertain generally to women (s 24(1B), (1C))
    `transgender grounds`           -- Part 3A (s 38A, s 38B)
    `marital or domestic status`    -- Part 4; single, married, separated, divorced, widowed or in a de facto relationship (s 4)
    `disability`                    -- Part 4A (s 4, s 49A, s 49B)
    `responsibilities as a carer`   -- Part 4B (s 49S, s 49T)
    `homosexuality`                 -- Part 4C (s 49ZF, s 49ZG)
    `age`                           -- Part 4G (s 49ZYA)

-- Whose characteristic the treatment was on the ground of: the aggrieved person's own, or that of a relative or
-- associate (s 4: a relative by blood, marriage, affinity or adoption, or a de facto partner; an associate is anyone
-- the person associates with socially, in business or otherwise, or who depends on or lives in the household of the
-- person).
DECLARE `Whose characteristic` IS ONE OF
    `my own`
    `a relative's or associate's`

-- s 4 "disability means" (a)-(e); s 49A: one the person has, is thought to have, had or is thought to have had, or will
-- have or is thought will have.
DECLARE `Kind of disability` IS ONE OF
    `total or partial loss of bodily or mental functions or of a part of the body`
    `organisms in the body causing or capable of causing disease or illness`
    `malfunction, malformation or disfigurement of a part of the body`
    `a disorder or malfunction resulting in learning differently`
    `a disorder, illness or disease affecting thought processes, perception of reality, emotions or judgment, or resulting in disturbed behaviour`
    `no condition of these kinds`

-- s 49S(1): the people a carer's responsibilities are for (with s 49S(2): responsibilities had, thought to be had,
-- had in the past or to be had in the future).
DECLARE `Person cared for` IS ONE OF
    `my child or step-child, who depends wholly or substantially on me or needs care or support`
    `a child or adult needing care or support, of whom I am guardian, for whom I have parental responsibility, or for whom I am an authorised carer`
    `an immediate family member needing care or support: a spouse or former spouse, or a grandchild, parent, grandparent, brother or sister (or step-relation) of mine or of my spouse or former spouse`
    `someone else`

-- s 38A: a transgender person, whether or not a recognised transgender person.
DECLARE `Transgender description` IS ONE OF
    `identifies as a member of the opposite sex by living, or seeking to live, as one`
    `has identified as a member of the opposite sex by living as one`
    `being of indeterminate sex, identifies as a member of a particular sex by living as one`
    `is thought of as a transgender person`
    `none of the transgender descriptions`

-- s 4 "homosexual means male or female homosexual"; s 49ZF: includes being thought to be.
DECLARE `Homosexuality description` IS ONE OF
    `is homosexual`
    `is thought to be homosexual`
    `is neither`

DECLARE `Characteristic facts` HAS
    `whose characteristic`          IS A `Whose characteristic`
    `the kind of disability`        IS A `Kind of disability`
    `the person cared for`          IS A `Person cared for`
    `the transgender description`   IS A `Transgender description`
    `the homosexuality description` IS A `Homosexuality description`

DECLARE `Treatment facts` HAS
    -- direct: s 7(1)(a), 24(1)(a), 38B(1)(a), 39(1)(a), 49B(1)(a), 49T(1)(a), 49ZG(1)(a), 49ZYA(1)(a)
    `treated less favourably than a comparable person without the characteristic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the treatment was on the ground of the characteristic`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(1)(b), race only
    `segregated on the ground of race`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- indirect: s 7(1)(c), 24(1)(b), 38B(1)(b), 39(1)(b), 49B(1)(b), 49T(1)(b), 49ZG(1)(b), 49ZYA(1)(b)
    `required to comply with a requirement or condition I do not or cannot comply with` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a substantially higher proportion of people without the characteristic comply or can comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 38B(1)(c), recognised transgender person only
    `I am a recognised transgender person`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `treated as being of my former sex`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a substantially higher proportion of people of my former sex comply or can comply` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A STRING
`the definition section for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `race` THEN "s 7"
    WHEN `sex` THEN "s 24"
    WHEN `transgender grounds` THEN "s 38B"
    WHEN `marital or domestic status` THEN "s 39"
    WHEN `disability` THEN "s 49B"
    WHEN `responsibilities as a carer` THEN "s 49T"
    WHEN `homosexuality` THEN "s 49ZG"
    WHEN `age` THEN "s 49ZYA"

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A STRING
`the work section for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `race` THEN "s 8"
    WHEN `sex` THEN "s 25"
    WHEN `transgender grounds` THEN "s 38C"
    WHEN `marital or domestic status` THEN "s 40"
    WHEN `disability` THEN "s 49D"
    WHEN `responsibilities as a carer` THEN "s 49V"
    WHEN `homosexuality` THEN "s 49ZH"
    WHEN `age` THEN "s 49ZYB"

-- Whether the person (or relative or associate) has the characteristic the ground needs. Race, sex, marital or
-- domestic status and age: everyone has one (the s 4 marital list covers every status). The other four need the
-- Act's definition to be met.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the characteristic is one the Act covers` g c IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `disability` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the kind of disability`
        WHEN `no condition of these kinds` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `responsibilities as a carer` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the person cared for`
        WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `transgender grounds` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the transgender description`
        WHEN `none of the transgender descriptions` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `homosexuality` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the homosexuality description`
        WHEN `is neither` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 49T(1) reaches only the aggrieved person's own responsibilities as a carer; every other ground extends to the
-- characteristic of a relative or associate.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whose characteristic counts` g c IF
    CONSIDER c's `whose characteristic`
    WHEN `my own` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a relative's or associate's` THEN (NOT (g EQUALS `responsibilities as a carer`))

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`, t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `direct discrimination` g c t IF
        `the characteristic is one the Act covers` g c
    AND `whose characteristic counts` g c
    AND t's `treated less favourably than a comparable person without the characteristic`
    AND t's `the treatment was on the ground of the characteristic`

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`, t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `segregation` g c t IF
        g EQUALS `race`
    AND t's `segregated on the ground of race`

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`, t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `indirect discrimination` g c t IF
        `the characteristic is one the Act covers` g c
    AND `whose characteristic counts` g c
    AND t's `required to comply with a requirement or condition I do not or cannot comply with`
    AND t's `a substantially higher proportion of people without the characteristic comply or can comply`
    AND t's `the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances`

-- s 38B(1)(c): treating a recognised transgender person as being of the former sex, or an unreasonable requirement
-- with which a substantially higher proportion of the former sex comply.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`, t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `former sex discrimination` g c t IF
        g EQUALS `transgender grounds`
    AND t's `I am a recognised transgender person`
    AND (    t's `treated as being of my former sex`
         OR (    t's `required to comply with a requirement or condition I do not or cannot comply with`
             AND t's `a substantially higher proportion of people of my former sex comply or can comply`
             AND t's `the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances`))

-- "A person (the perpetrator) discriminates against another person (the aggrieved person) on the ground of ... if
-- the perpetrator ..." (each definition section): the list is the definition, so failing it is the text's no.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`, t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `discriminates` g c t IF
       `direct discrimination` g c t
    OR `segregation` g c t
    OR `indirect discrimination` g c t
    OR `former sex discrimination` g c t

§ `Discrimination in work: applicants and employees`

-- s 8(1), (2) and the matching subsections of ss 25, 38C, 40, 49D, 49V, 49ZH, 49ZYB. "employment includes work under
-- a contract for services" (s 4).
DECLARE `What the employer did` IS ONE OF
    `discriminated in its arrangements for deciding who should be offered employment`
    `discriminated in deciding who should be offered employment`
    `discriminated in the terms on which it offered me employment`
    `discriminated in the terms or conditions of my employment`
    `denied or limited my access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits of employment`
    `dismissed me`
    `subjected me to some other detriment`

DECLARE `Employer facts` HAS
    `the employment is for the purposes of the employer's private household`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of people the employer employs`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the employer is a private educational authority`                         IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Exception facts` HAS
    `it was necessary to comply with another Act, an instrument under one, or an order of the Tribunal or a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a religious bodies exception applies`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person of a particular race is required for authenticity, or for welfare services best given by a person of that race` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am not ordinarily resident in NSW and the job trains me in skills to be used wholly outside NSW` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the job is on a ship or aircraft and I was engaged for it outside NSW`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was a special needs program for people of a particular race or age group` IS A BOOLEAN
    `being of a particular sex or age is a genuine occupational qualification for the job` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a man and it was a grant to a woman of rights connected with pregnancy, childbirth or breastfeeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it concerned superannuation fund terms that meet the Act's superannuation exception` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the job is one of two to be held by a married couple`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disability is an infectious disease and it was reasonably necessary to protect public health` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disability relates to my addiction to a prohibited drug and I was actually addicted at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I would be unable to carry out the inherent requirements of the job`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I would need services, facilities or arrangements that would impose unjustifiable hardship on the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was under 21`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was an offer, by length of service, to join a voluntary retirement or severance scheme` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Work answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: this is unlawful discrimination in work` HAS `under` IS A STRING
    `no: this is not discrimination as the Act defines it` HAS `under` IS A STRING
    `no: the section does not apply to this employment` HAS `because` IS A STRING
    `no: an exception makes it lawful` HAS `under` IS A STRING

GIVEN s IS A `What the employer did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was about an applicant` s IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `discriminated in its arrangements for deciding who should be offered employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `discriminated in deciding who should be offered employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `discriminated in the terms on which it offered me employment` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ss 49D(4) and 49V(4) reach only s (1)(b) (deciding who should be offered employment) and s (2)(c) (dismissal).
GIVEN s IS A `What the employer did`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was hiring or dismissal` s IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `discriminated in deciding who should be offered employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dismissed me` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The exclusions in s 8(3), 25(3), 38C(3), 40(3), 49D(3), 49V(3), 49ZH(3), 49ZYB(3): "do not apply to employment".
-- Private household: every ground. Five or fewer employees (counting related bodies corporate, s 25(4) etc.): not
-- race and not age. Private educational authority: not race, not carers, not age.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, e IS A `Employer facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the exclusion that applies` g e MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF e's `the employment is for the purposes of the employer's private household`
        THEN JUST (CONCAT `the household subsection`, ": the employment is for the purposes of a private household")
        IF `the small employer exclusion reaches` g AND e's `the number of people the employer employs` AT MOST 5
        THEN JUST (CONCAT (`the work section for` g), "(3)(b): the employer employs no more than 5 people (not counting its private household, and counting related bodies corporate)")
        IF `the private educational authority exclusion reaches` g AND e's `the employer is a private educational authority`
        THEN JUST (CONCAT (`the work section for` g), "(3)(c): the employer is a private educational authority")
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the household subsection` MEANS
            IF g EQUALS `race` OR g EQUALS `age`
            THEN CONCAT (`the work section for` g), "(3)"
            ELSE CONCAT (`the work section for` g), "(3)(a)"

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the small employer exclusion reaches` g IF
    (NOT (g EQUALS `race` OR g EQUALS `age`))

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the private educational authority exclusion reaches` g IF
    (NOT (g EQUALS `race` OR g EQUALS `age` OR g EQUALS `responsibilities as a carer`))

-- The exceptions that reach an applicant's or employee's claim, each in the text's words "nothing in this Division /
-- Part / Act applies to / renders unlawful / affects". Checked in the order the Act prints them (ground-specific
-- first, then Part 6); the first that applies is named.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`, s IS A `What the employer did`, x IS A `Exception facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the exception that applies` g c s x MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND x's `a person of a particular race is required for authenticity, or for welfare services best given by a person of that race`
        THEN JUST "s 14 (genuine occupational qualification: race)"
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND x's `I am not ordinarily resident in NSW and the job trains me in skills to be used wholly outside NSW`
        THEN JUST "s 15 (employment to train in skills to be used outside New South Wales)"
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND x's `the job is on a ship or aircraft and I was engaged for it outside NSW`
        THEN JUST "s 16 (employment on a ship or aircraft, engaged outside New South Wales)"
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND x's `it was a special needs program for people of a particular race or age group`
        THEN JUST "s 21 (special needs programs and activities)"
        IF g EQUALS `sex` AND x's `being of a particular sex or age is a genuine occupational qualification for the job`
        THEN JUST "s 31 (genuine occupational qualification: sex)"
        IF g EQUALS `sex` AND x's `I am a man and it was a grant to a woman of rights connected with pregnancy, childbirth or breastfeeding`
        THEN JUST "s 35 (rights or privileges in connection with pregnancy, childbirth or breastfeeding)"
        IF g EQUALS `sex` AND x's `it concerned superannuation fund terms that meet the Act's superannuation exception`
        THEN JUST "s 36 (superannuation)"
        IF g EQUALS `transgender grounds` AND x's `it concerned superannuation fund terms that meet the Act's superannuation exception`
        THEN JUST "s 38Q (superannuation)"
        IF g EQUALS `marital or domestic status` AND x's `the job is one of two to be held by a married couple`
        THEN JUST "s 46 (employment of a married couple)"
        IF g EQUALS `marital or domestic status` AND x's `it concerned superannuation fund terms that meet the Act's superannuation exception`
        THEN JUST "s 49 (superannuation)"
        IF g EQUALS `disability` AND `it was hiring or dismissal` s AND `the inherent requirements test is met` x
        THEN JUST "s 49D(4) (inherent requirements of the employment, or unjustifiable hardship)"
        IF g EQUALS `disability` AND x's `the disability is an infectious disease and it was reasonably necessary to protect public health`
        THEN JUST "s 49P (public health)"
        IF g EQUALS `disability` AND x's `the disability relates to my addiction to a prohibited drug and I was actually addicted at the time`
        THEN JUST "s 49PA (persons addicted to prohibited drugs)"
        IF g EQUALS `disability` AND x's `it concerned superannuation fund terms that meet the Act's superannuation exception`
        THEN JUST "s 49Q (superannuation, insurance)"
        IF g EQUALS `responsibilities as a carer` AND `it was hiring or dismissal` s AND `the inherent requirements test is met` x
        THEN JUST "s 49V(4) (inherent requirements of the employment, or unjustifiable hardship)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND x's `I was under 21` AND `it was about an applicant` s
        THEN JUST "s 49ZYI(1) (junior employees: offering employment to a person under 21)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND x's `I was under 21` AND s EQUALS `discriminated in the terms or conditions of my employment`
        THEN JUST "s 49ZYI(2) (junior employees: terms or conditions of an employee under 21)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND x's `being of a particular sex or age is a genuine occupational qualification for the job`
        THEN JUST "s 49ZYJ (genuine occupational qualification: age)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND x's `it was an offer, by length of service, to join a voluntary retirement or severance scheme`
        THEN JUST "s 49ZYK (voluntary retirement or severance schemes)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND x's `it was a special needs program for people of a particular race or age group`
        THEN JUST "s 49ZYR (special needs programs and activities)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND x's `it concerned superannuation fund terms that meet the Act's superannuation exception`
        THEN JUST "s 49ZYS (superannuation)"
        IF x's `it was necessary to comply with another Act, an instrument under one, or an order of the Tribunal or a court`
        THEN JUST "s 54 (acts done under statutory authority)"
        IF x's `a religious bodies exception applies`
        THEN JUST "s 56 (religious bodies)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- ss 49D(4), 49V(4): (a) unable to carry out the inherent requirements, or (b) would need services, facilities or
-- arrangements not needed by others whose provision would impose unjustifiable hardship (s 49C, s 49U).
GIVEN x IS A `Exception facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inherent requirements test is met` x IF
       x's `I would be unable to carry out the inherent requirements of the job`
    OR x's `I would need services, facilities or arrangements that would impose unjustifiable hardship on the employer`

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, c IS A `Characteristic facts`, t IS A `Treatment facts`, s IS A `What the employer did`, e IS A `Employer facts`, x IS A `Exception facts`
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`the answer on discrimination in work` g c t s e x MEANS
    IF (NOT (`discriminates` g c t))
    THEN `no: this is not discrimination as the Act defines it` (`the definition section for` g)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the exclusion that applies` g e
         WHEN JUST r THEN `no: the section does not apply to this employment` r
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `the exception that applies` g c s x
             WHEN JUST r THEN `no: an exception makes it lawful` r
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `yes: this is unlawful discrimination in work` (CONCAT (`the work section for` g), `the subsection`)
    WHERE
        `the subsection` MEANS IF `it was about an applicant` s THEN "(1)" ELSE "(2)"

§ `Part 2A: sexual harassment at work`

DECLARE `Sexual conduct` IS ONE OF
    `an unwelcome sexual advance`
    `an unwelcome request for sexual favours`
    `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`
    `no unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`

-- s 22B(1)-(7), from the seat of the person harassed. s 22B(8) (a workplace participant harassing a member of
-- Parliament) and ss 22C-22J (other areas) are not encoded.
DECLARE `Who harassed me` IS ONE OF
    `my employer, while I was its employee or was seeking employment with it`
    `a fellow employee, while I was employed by or seeking employment with the same employer`
    `a person whose commission agent or contract worker I am or was seeking to become`
    `a fellow commission agent or contract worker`
    `another partner in a partnership of which I was a partner or was seeking to become one`
    `another workplace participant, at a place that is a workplace of both of us, while I was a workplace participant`
    `a member of Parliament, at a place that is a workplace of both of us, while I was a workplace participant or member`
    `someone else, or somewhere else`

DECLARE `Harassment answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: this is unlawful sexual harassment` HAS `under` IS A STRING
    `no: this is not sexual harassment as s 22A defines it`
    `s 22B does not reach this: the work relationships it covers do not include this one (Part 2A's other areas, ss 22C-22J, are not encoded here)`

-- s 22A: "a person sexually harasses another person if (a) ... or (b) ... in circumstances in which a reasonable
-- person ... would have anticipated that the other person would be offended, humiliated or intimidated".
GIVEN k IS A `Sexual conduct`, `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence, humiliation or intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sexually harasses` k `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence, humiliation or intimidation` IF
        `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence, humiliation or intimidation`
    AND CONSIDER k
        WHEN `no unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN h IS A `Who harassed me`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the s 22B subsection for` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `my employer, while I was its employee or was seeking employment with it` THEN JUST "s 22B(1)"
    WHEN `a fellow employee, while I was employed by or seeking employment with the same employer` THEN JUST "s 22B(2)"
    WHEN `a person whose commission agent or contract worker I am or was seeking to become` THEN JUST "s 22B(3)"
    WHEN `a fellow commission agent or contract worker` THEN JUST "s 22B(4)"
    WHEN `another partner in a partnership of which I was a partner or was seeking to become one` THEN JUST "s 22B(5)"
    WHEN `another workplace participant, at a place that is a workplace of both of us, while I was a workplace participant` THEN JUST "s 22B(6)"
    WHEN `a member of Parliament, at a place that is a workplace of both of us, while I was a workplace participant or member` THEN JUST "s 22B(7)"
    WHEN `someone else, or somewhere else` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN k IS A `Sexual conduct`, r IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A `Who harassed me`
GIVETH A `Harassment answer`
`the answer on sexual harassment at work` k r h MEANS
    IF (NOT (`sexually harasses` k r))
    THEN `no: this is not sexual harassment as s 22A defines it`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the s 22B subsection for` h
         WHEN JUST sub THEN `yes: this is unlawful sexual harassment` sub
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 22B does not reach this: the work relationships it covers do not include this one (Part 2A's other areas, ss 22C-22J, are not encoded here)`

§ `Part 4E: compulsory retirement on the ground of age`

DECLARE `Retirement conduct` IS ONE OF
    `retired me`
    `required me to retire`
    `threatened to retire me`
    `engaged in conduct with a view to causing me to retire`
    `none of these retirement acts`

-- s 49ZX: the retirements to which Part 4E does not apply.
DECLARE `My office` IS ONE OF
    `none of the excepted offices`
    `a judicial officer`
    `a prosecutor, public defender or Solicitor General listed in s 49ZX(b)`
    `an officer removable only with the involvement of Parliament and not appointed for a term`
    `an office or person prescribed by regulation`

DECLARE `Retirement answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is unlawful to retire you, require or threaten your retirement, or act to cause it, on the ground of your age (s 49ZV), despite any retirement age in an award or agreement (s 49ZU(2)); a statutory retirement age for a public sector employee has no effect (s 49ZW)`
    `no: Part 4E does not apply to the retirement of the holder of your office (s 49ZX)`
    `Part 4E does not reach this: it protects employees in New South Wales, including commission agents and contract workers (s 49ZU)`
    `s 49ZV does not reach this: it makes unlawful only retiring an employee, requiring or threatening retirement, or acting to cause it, on the ground of age`

GIVEN `I am an employee in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN, o IS A `My office`, k IS A `Retirement conduct`, `it was on the ground of my age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Retirement answer`
`the answer on compulsory retirement` `I am an employee in New South Wales` o k `it was on the ground of my age` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am an employee in New South Wales`)
    THEN `Part 4E does not reach this: it protects employees in New South Wales, including commission agents and contract workers (s 49ZU)`
    ELSE IF (NOT (o EQUALS `none of the excepted offices`))
         THEN `no: Part 4E does not apply to the retirement of the holder of your office (s 49ZX)`
         ELSE IF (NOT (k EQUALS `none of these retirement acts`)) AND `it was on the ground of my age`
              THEN `yes: it is unlawful to retire you, require or threaten your retirement, or act to cause it, on the ground of your age (s 49ZV), despite any retirement age in an award or agreement (s 49ZU(2)); a statutory retirement age for a public sector employee has no effect (s 49ZW)`
              ELSE `s 49ZV does not reach this: it makes unlawful only retiring an employee, requiring or threatening retirement, or acting to cause it, on the ground of age`

§ `Part 5: victimisation and the liability of employers`

-- s 50(1)(a)-(d) and the closing words.
DECLARE `What I did under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `I brought proceedings under the Act`
    `I gave evidence or information in connection with proceedings under the Act`
    `I alleged that someone had done something that would contravene the Act`
    `I did something else under or by reference to the Act`
    `they knew I intended to do one of these, or suspected I had done or intended to do one`
    `nothing under the Act`

DECLARE `Victimisation answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: subjecting you to a detriment on that ground is unlawful victimisation (s 50(1))`
    `no: s 50(1) does not apply to a detriment because of an allegation that was false and not made in good faith (s 50(2))`
    `s 50 does not reach this: it makes unlawful a detriment imposed on the ground that you did, intended or were suspected of something under the Act`

GIVEN `I was subjected to a detriment` IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A `What I did under the Act`, `the detriment was on the ground of it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the allegation was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `the allegation was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Victimisation answer`
`the answer on victimisation` `I was subjected to a detriment` p `the detriment was on the ground of it` `the allegation was false` `the allegation was made in good faith` MEANS
    IF `I was subjected to a detriment` AND `the detriment was on the ground of it` AND (NOT (p EQUALS `nothing under the Act`))
    THEN IF p EQUALS `I alleged that someone had done something that would contravene the Act` AND `the allegation was false` AND (NOT `the allegation was made in good faith`)
         THEN `no: s 50(1) does not apply to a detriment because of an allegation that was false and not made in good faith (s 50(2))`
         ELSE `yes: subjecting you to a detriment on that ground is unlawful victimisation (s 50(1))`
    ELSE `s 50 does not reach this: it makes unlawful a detriment imposed on the ground that you did, intended or were suspected of something under the Act`

DECLARE `Employer liability answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the act is taken to have been done by the employer or principal too, and you may hold both liable, jointly and severally (s 53(1), (2))`
    `no: the employer or principal did not authorise the act, expressly or by implication, before or after it (s 53(1))`
    `no: the employer or principal took all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention (s 53(3))`
    `s 53 does not reach this: it makes an employer or principal answer only for an act its employee or agent did as such that would contravene the Act if the employer had done it`

-- s 53(1): an act done "as the agent or employee" that would contravene the Act if the employer did it "is taken to
-- have been done by the principal or employer also unless the principal or employer did not ... authorise" it; (3)
-- "Despite subsection (1)" no liability where all reasonable steps were taken. The onus of an exception is on the
-- respondent (s 104). For a volunteer or unpaid trainee who sexually harassed, the principal is the body for whom they
-- provide services (s 53(4)).
GIVEN `the person acted as the employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN, `it would contravene the Act if the employer did it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer took all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Employer liability answer`
`the answer on the employer's liability` `the person acted as the employee or agent` `it would contravene the Act if the employer did it` `the employer authorised it` `the employer took all reasonable steps to prevent it` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the person acted as the employee or agent` AND `it would contravene the Act if the employer did it`))
    THEN `s 53 does not reach this: it makes an employer or principal answer only for an act its employee or agent did as such that would contravene the Act if the employer had done it`
    ELSE IF (NOT `the employer authorised it`)
         THEN `no: the employer or principal did not authorise the act, expressly or by implication, before or after it (s 53(1))`
         ELSE IF `the employer took all reasonable steps to prevent it`
              THEN `no: the employer or principal took all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention (s 53(3))`
              ELSE `yes: the act is taken to have been done by the employer or principal too, and you may hold both liable, jointly and severally (s 53(1), (2))`

§ `Part 9: making a complaint`

-- s 87A(1)(a)-(d).
DECLARE `Who makes the complaint` IS ONE OF
    `I do, for myself`
    `I do, for myself and on behalf of others`
    `a parent or guardian, for a person who lacks the legal capacity to complain`
    `a representative body, on behalf of named people`
    `an agent, such as a lawyer, for one of these`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Standing answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the complaint may be made (s 87A(1)(a))`
    `yes: the complaint may be made on behalf of others too (s 87A(1)(a)(ii)); the Tribunal decides whether it goes on as a representative complaint (s 101)`
    `yes: a parent or guardian may complain for a person who lacks legal capacity (s 87A(1)(b))`
    `yes: the representative body may complain, having satisfied the President of each person's consent and its sufficient interest (s 87A(1)(c), s 87C)`
    `no: a representative body may complain only after satisfying the President that each person consents and that it has a sufficient interest (s 87C(1))`
    `yes: an agent may make the complaint (s 87A(1)(d))`
    `no: a complaint may be made only by the people s 87A(1) lists`
    `no: a complaint cannot be made about a contravention of a provision for which a specific penalty is imposed (s 87A(1)); that is for a prosecution, and the President may decline such a complaint (s 89B(2)(c))`

GIVEN w IS A `Who makes the complaint`, `the provision carries a specific penalty` IS A BOOLEAN, `each person consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President is satisfied the body has a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Standing answer`
`the answer on who may complain` w `the provision carries a specific penalty` `each person consents` `the President is satisfied the body has a sufficient interest` MEANS
    IF `the provision carries a specific penalty`
    THEN `no: a complaint cannot be made about a contravention of a provision for which a specific penalty is imposed (s 87A(1)); that is for a prosecution, and the President may decline such a complaint (s 89B(2)(c))`
    ELSE CONSIDER w
         WHEN `I do, for myself` THEN `yes: the complaint may be made (s 87A(1)(a))`
         WHEN `I do, for myself and on behalf of others` THEN `yes: the complaint may be made on behalf of others too (s 87A(1)(a)(ii)); the Tribunal decides whether it goes on as a representative complaint (s 101)`
         WHEN `a parent or guardian, for a person who lacks the legal capacity to complain` THEN `yes: a parent or guardian may complain for a person who lacks legal capacity (s 87A(1)(b))`
         WHEN `a representative body, on behalf of named people` THEN
             IF `each person consents` AND `the President is satisfied the body has a sufficient interest`
             THEN `yes: the representative body may complain, having satisfied the President of each person's consent and its sufficient interest (s 87A(1)(c), s 87C)`
             ELSE `no: a representative body may complain only after satisfying the President that each person consents and that it has a sufficient interest (s 87C(1))`
         WHEN `an agent, such as a lawyer, for one of these` THEN `yes: an agent may make the complaint (s 87A(1)(d))`
         WHEN `someone else` THEN `no: a complaint may be made only by the people s 87A(1) lists`

§§ `The complainant's steps with deadlines, as regulative rules`

DECLARE `Complaint party` IS ONE OF `the complainant`

DECLARE `Complainant step` IS ONE OF
    `lodge the complaint with the President`
    `require the President to refer the complaint to the Tribunal`
    `apply to the Tribunal to register the conciliation agreement`
    `satisfy the President that the abandoned complaint should be revived`

-- s 89B(2)(b): a complaint about conduct that occurred more than 12 months before it was made may be declined. Not a
-- duty: the breach here means only that the President may decline (fork F5).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Complaint party` `Complainant step`
`the complaint should be lodged within 12 months of the conduct` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the complainant`
    MUST   `lodge the complaint with the President`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint was made, so the President may decline the complaint (s 89B(2)(b))"

-- s 93A(1): within 21 days after a notice declining the complaint (s 87B(4) or s 92) is given.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Complaint party` `Complainant step`
`the referral must be required within 21 days of the notice` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the complainant`
    MUST   `require the President to refer the complaint to the Tribunal`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "the complainant did not require referral within 21 days after the notice declining the complaint was given (s 93A(1))"

-- s 91A(6): not later than 6 months after the date of the agreement.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Complaint party` `Complainant step`
`the registration application must be made within 6 months of the agreement` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the complainant`
    MUST   `apply to the Tribunal to register the conciliation agreement`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "the application to register the conciliation agreement was made more than 6 months after the agreement (s 91A(6))"

-- s 92C(2): within 12 months after the end of the 28-day period in the abandonment notice.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Complaint party` `Complainant step`
`the revival must be sought within 12 months after the 28 days` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the complainant`
    MUST   `satisfy the President that the abandoned complaint should be revived`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "the complainant did not satisfy the President within 12 months after the end of the 28-day period (s 92C(2))"

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. Clock: day 0 is the day the period
-- starts; the step is taken on day (the day taken minus the start). Takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Complaint party` `Complainant step`, step IS A `Complainant step`, `the start` IS A DATE, `the day taken` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step was in time under` `the rule` step `from` `the start` `taken on` `the day taken` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the complainant` step (`the days from` `the start` `to` `the day taken`)))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Lodging the complaint in time (s 89B(2)(b))`

-- "more than 12 months before the making of the complaint": conduct on day D is not more than 12 months before a
-- complaint made on or before D plus 12 months (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of the earliest conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to lodge for conduct on` `the day of the earliest conduct` MEANS `the day of the earliest conduct` `plus months` 12

GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE, `the day lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `conduct on` `the day of the conduct` `is within 12 months of a complaint on` `the day lodged` IF
    `the step was in time under` (`the complaint should be lodged within 12 months of the conduct` (`the days from` `the day of the conduct` `to` (`the last day to lodge for conduct on` `the day of the conduct`))) `lodge the complaint with the President` `from` `the day of the conduct` `taken on` `the day lodged`

DECLARE `Complaint time answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: no part of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so s 89B(2)(b) gives no ground to decline it`
    `partly late: part of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so the President may (but need not) decline the complaint in whole or in part (s 89B(1), (2)(b))`
    `late: all of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so the President may (but need not) decline it (s 89B(2)(b))`

GIVEN `the day of the earliest conduct` IS A DATE, `the day of the latest conduct` IS A DATE, `the day lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Complaint time answer`
`the answer on lodging in time` `the day of the earliest conduct` `the day of the latest conduct` `the day lodged` MEANS
    IF `conduct on` `the day of the earliest conduct` `is within 12 months of a complaint on` `the day lodged`
    THEN `in time: no part of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so s 89B(2)(b) gives no ground to decline it`
    ELSE IF `conduct on` `the day of the latest conduct` `is within 12 months of a complaint on` `the day lodged`
         THEN `partly late: part of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so the President may (but need not) decline the complaint in whole or in part (s 89B(1), (2)(b))`
         ELSE `late: all of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so the President may (but need not) decline it (s 89B(2)(b))`

§§ `Requiring referral after a decline (s 93A, s 94B)`

-- s 93A(1): "within 21 days after the date on which the notice was given": the day of giving is not counted (fork F2),
-- so the last day is that day plus 21. s 94B(1): for a notice given by post the period "is ... taken to run from, and
-- includes, the seventh working day after the notice was posted", so the last day is that working day plus 20 (fork F3).
-- Weekday public or bank holidays in the place the notice was sent to are an input: each pushes the seventh working
-- day back by one.
GIVEN `it was posted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day given or posted` IS A DATE, `weekday holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the 21 days start` `it was posted` `the day given or posted` `weekday holidays` MEANS
    IF `it was posted`
    THEN `the weekday number` (7 PLUS `weekday holidays`) `after` `the day given or posted`
    ELSE `the day given or posted` `plus days` 1

GIVEN `it was posted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day given or posted` IS A DATE, `weekday holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to require referral` `it was posted` `the day given or posted` `weekday holidays` MEANS
    (`the day the 21 days start` `it was posted` `the day given or posted` `weekday holidays`) `plus days` 20

DECLARE `Referral answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the President must refer the complaint to the Tribunal (s 93A(2)); the Tribunal's leave is needed before it can be the subject of proceedings (s 96(1))`
    `late: the 21 days after the notice declining the complaint have passed (s 93A(1))`

GIVEN `it was posted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day given or posted` IS A DATE, `weekday holidays` IS A NUMBER, `the day I required referral` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Referral answer`
`the answer on requiring referral` `it was posted` `the day given or posted` `weekday holidays` `the day I required referral` MEANS
    IF `the step was in time under` (`the referral must be required within 21 days of the notice` (`the days from` `the day given or posted` `to` (`the last day to require referral` `it was posted` `the day given or posted` `weekday holidays`))) `require the President to refer the complaint to the Tribunal` `from` `the day given or posted` `taken on` `the day I required referral`
    THEN `in time: the President must refer the complaint to the Tribunal (s 93A(2)); the Tribunal's leave is needed before it can be the subject of proceedings (s 96(1))`
    ELSE `late: the 21 days after the notice declining the complaint have passed (s 93A(1))`

§§ `Referral of an unresolved complaint after 18 months (s 93B)`

-- "not ... resolved within 18 months after the date on which it was made": the 18 months end on the same day of the
-- month 18 months later (fork F1); a request can be made from the next day (fork F4).
GIVEN `the day the complaint was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day to request referral of an unresolved complaint made on` `the day the complaint was made` MEANS
    (`the day the complaint was made` `plus months` 18) `plus days` 1

DECLARE `Who asked for referral` IS ONE OF `I asked`, `the respondent asked`

DECLARE `Unresolved referral answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: a party may request referral only if the complaint has not been declined, terminated or otherwise resolved within 18 months after it was made (s 93B(1))`
    `not yet: a party may request referral only once 18 months after the complaint was made have passed (s 93B(1))`
    `referred: no party objected within 28 days after the President gave notice of the request, so the President is to refer the complaint (s 93B(3))`
    `not referred: because you objected the President must not refer it, and may terminate it if satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(4))`
    `referred: the respondent objected, but the President is to refer it unless satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(5))`
    `not referred: the respondent objected and the President is satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(5))`

GIVEN `the complaint was resolved within 18 months` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the complaint was made` IS A DATE, `the day of the request` IS A DATE, a IS A `Who asked for referral`, `I objected` IS A BOOLEAN, `the respondent objected` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President is satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Unresolved referral answer`
`the answer on referral of an unresolved complaint` `the complaint was resolved within 18 months` `the day the complaint was made` `the day of the request` a `I objected` `the respondent objected` `the President is satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement` MEANS
    IF `the complaint was resolved within 18 months`
    THEN `no: a party may request referral only if the complaint has not been declined, terminated or otherwise resolved within 18 months after it was made (s 93B(1))`
    ELSE IF (NOT ((`the first day to request referral of an unresolved complaint made on` `the day the complaint was made`) `is on or before` `the day of the request`))
         THEN `not yet: a party may request referral only once 18 months after the complaint was made have passed (s 93B(1))`
         ELSE IF `I objected` AND a EQUALS `the respondent asked`
              THEN `not referred: because you objected the President must not refer it, and may terminate it if satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(4))`
              ELSE IF `the respondent objected` AND a EQUALS `I asked`
                   THEN IF `the President is satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement`
                        THEN `not referred: the respondent objected and the President is satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(5))`
                        ELSE `referred: the respondent objected, but the President is to refer it unless satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(5))`
                   ELSE `referred: no party objected within 28 days after the President gave notice of the request, so the President is to refer the complaint (s 93B(3))`

§§ `Registering a conciliation agreement (s 91A(5)-(9))`

GIVEN `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to register an agreement made on` `the day of the agreement` MEANS `the day of the agreement` `plus months` 6

DECLARE `Registration answer` IS ONE OF
    `you may apply: serve the application and the agreement on each other party (s 91A(7)); if the Tribunal is satisfied a party has not complied, it is to register the provisions it could have ordered, which then take effect as its order (s 91A(8), (9))`
    `no: only a written, signed record of an agreement reached after conciliation can be registered (s 91A(5), (6))`
    `no: an application may be made only by a party who is of the opinion that another party has not complied with the agreement (s 91A(6))`
    `late: the application must be made not later than 6 months after the date of the agreement (s 91A(6))`

GIVEN `the agreement is recorded in writing and signed` IS A BOOLEAN, `I think another party has not complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE, `the day I apply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Registration answer`
`the answer on registering the agreement` `the agreement is recorded in writing and signed` `I think another party has not complied` `the day of the agreement` `the day I apply` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the agreement is recorded in writing and signed`)
    THEN `no: only a written, signed record of an agreement reached after conciliation can be registered (s 91A(5), (6))`
    ELSE IF (NOT `I think another party has not complied`)
         THEN `no: an application may be made only by a party who is of the opinion that another party has not complied with the agreement (s 91A(6))`
         ELSE IF `the step was in time under` (`the registration application must be made within 6 months of the agreement` (`the days from` `the day of the agreement` `to` (`the last day to apply to register an agreement made on` `the day of the agreement`))) `apply to the Tribunal to register the conciliation agreement` `from` `the day of the agreement` `taken on` `the day I apply`
              THEN `you may apply: serve the application and the agreement on each other party (s 91A(7)); if the Tribunal is satisfied a party has not complied, it is to register the provisions it could have ordered, which then take effect as its order (s 91A(8), (9))`
              ELSE `late: the application must be made not later than 6 months after the date of the agreement (s 91A(6))`

§§ `Reviving an abandoned complaint (s 92C)`

-- The 28-day period ends 28 days after the notice was served (the day of service not counted, fork F2); revival is
-- possible within 12 months after that (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day the notice was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to revive a complaint whose abandonment notice was served on` `the day the notice was served` MEANS
    (`the day the notice was served` `plus days` 28) `plus months` 12

DECLARE `Revival answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the complaint may be revived (s 92C(2))`
    `no: the President must be satisfied that you wish to pursue it, that the failure did not happen or ought reasonably to be excused, and that reviving it causes the respondent no undue prejudice (s 92C(2))`
    `late: a complaint taken to be abandoned may be revived only within 12 months after the end of the 28-day period (s 92C(2))`

GIVEN `the day the notice was served` IS A DATE, `the day I satisfy the President` IS A DATE, `the President is satisfied of all three matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Revival answer`
`the answer on reviving the complaint` `the day the notice was served` `the day I satisfy the President` `the President is satisfied of all three matters` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the step was in time under` (`the revival must be sought within 12 months after the 28 days` (`the days from` `the day the notice was served` `to` (`the last day to revive a complaint whose abandonment notice was served on` `the day the notice was served`))) `satisfy the President that the abandoned complaint should be revived` `from` `the day the notice was served` `taken on` `the day I satisfy the President`))
    THEN `late: a complaint taken to be abandoned may be revived only within 12 months after the end of the 28-day period (s 92C(2))`
    ELSE IF `the President is satisfied of all three matters`
         THEN `yes: the complaint may be revived (s 92C(2))`
         ELSE `no: the President must be satisfied that you wish to pursue it, that the failure did not happen or ought reasonably to be excused, and that reviving it causes the respondent no undue prejudice (s 92C(2))`

§ `Part 9: what the Tribunal may order (s 108)`

`the damages cap` MEANS 100000

-- s 108(2)(a): damages "not exceeding $100,000 by way of compensation for any loss or damage", except on a matter the
-- Minister referred (s 95(2)). The loss is the Tribunal's assessment, an input.
GIVEN `the Minister referred the matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `the loss the Tribunal finds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Tribunal may order for my loss` `the Minister referred the matter` `the loss the Tribunal finds` MEANS
    IF `the Minister referred the matter`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the smaller of` `the loss the Tribunal finds` `and` `the damages cap`

-- s 108(7): where an order under s 108(2)(b)-(e) is made, the Tribunal may also order that in default of compliance the
-- respondent pay damages "not exceeding $100,000 by way of compensation for failure to comply". Not barred on a
-- Minister's referral (finding 3).
GIVEN `a default order was made and not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN, `the loss from the failure to comply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most for failure to comply` `a default order was made and not complied with` `the loss from the failure to comply` MEANS
    IF `a default order was made and not complied with`
    THEN `the smaller of` `the loss from the failure to comply` `and` `the damages cap`
    ELSE 0

DECLARE `Who receives the damages` IS ONE OF
    `you: damages ordered carry interest from the date the order takes effect (or an earlier date the Tribunal orders) at the District Court judgment rate (s 112)`
    `you, not the representative body that complained for you: the Tribunal may direct how the damages are applied for your benefit (s 108(4), (5)); interest runs as for any damages (s 112)`
    `not you: a protected defendant must pay damages for conduct while you were an offender in custody into the Victims Support Fund, which discharges its liability to you (s 111A)`

GIVEN `a representative body made the complaint` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was conduct of a protected defendant while I was an offender in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who receives the damages`
`the answer on who receives the damages` `a representative body made the complaint` `it was conduct of a protected defendant while I was an offender in custody` MEANS
    IF `it was conduct of a protected defendant while I was an offender in custody`
    THEN `not you: a protected defendant must pay damages for conduct while you were an offender in custody into the Victims Support Fund, which discharges its liability to you (s 111A)`
    ELSE IF `a representative body made the complaint`
         THEN `you, not the representative body that complained for you: the Tribunal may direct how the damages are applied for your benefit (s 108(4), (5)); interest runs as for any damages (s 112)`
         ELSE `you: damages ordered carry interest from the date the order takes effect (or an earlier date the Tribunal orders) at the District Court judgment rate (s 112)`
